From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:33:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: apple: pmp-report: vote the AGX request by default

Set pmp_report.agx_vote to on by default. While GPU work is in flight,
the report then sets the AGX power request and acknowledges it, and
clears it 250 ms after the last operation (pmp-agx-vote.h). The vote
only reaches a report that has a qualified AGX record: T6001 record 9,
or the J604 record of device ID 5 that apple_pmp_t8132_agx_bit() reads
from the PMP's soc-device table. On every other machine agx_id is -1
and the default changes nothing.

To roll back at runtime, write 0 to
/sys/module/pmp_report/parameters/agx_vote. The setter clears a held
request at once. To roll back at boot, pass pmp_report.agx_vote=0.

[j604: HOLD. Take this into 1.612 only after the AGX vote measurement on the
J604 shows VOTE WORKS, GAIN >= +5 % read or write, and IDLE not
regressed. No such run exists yet: every logged run so far stopped in
its dry mode before measuring.]

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
index 24aee54dd1..072eac5fe3 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
@@ -89,7 +89,7 @@ static const struct apple_pmp_report_offsets apple_pmp_offsets_t8132;
 
 /* T6001 AGX request (see the engine below set_state): AGX is soc-device record 9 on the T6001. */
 #define APPLE_PMP_T6001_AGX_ID 9
-static bool agx_vote;
+static bool agx_vote = true;
 static struct agx_vote apple_pmp_agx_vote_state = {.idle_ms = AGX_VOTE_IDLE_MS_DEFAULT};
 static DEFINE_SPINLOCK(apple_pmp_agx_vote_lock);
 /* Serializes the vote work, the unbind release and the report's removal. */
@@ -1379,7 +1379,7 @@ static int apple_pmp_report_set_state(struct apple_pmp_report *rep, u32 id,
  * leaves memory at its idle floor for a GPU that is busy but has not asked. The GPU driver reports operations in flight
  * (apple_pmp_agx_activity_begin/end); the request is set while any operation runs and cleared agx_vote_idle_ms after the last one ends, at
  * GPU unbind and when this report goes away. The decisions are in pmp-agx-vote.h (unit tested); this is the glue.
- * Off by default (pmp_report.agx_vote): with it off nothing is written.
+ * On by default (pmp_report.agx_vote); with it off nothing is written.
  */
 static unsigned int agx_vote_idle_ms = AGX_VOTE_IDLE_MS_DEFAULT;
 
@@ -1417,7 +1417,7 @@ static const struct kernel_param_ops apple_pmp_agx_vote_ops = {
 };
 module_param_cb(agx_vote, &apple_pmp_agx_vote_ops, &agx_vote, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(agx_vote,
-	"Set the AGX power request while GPU work is in flight (T6001, J604; default: off)");
+	"Set the AGX power request while GPU work is in flight (T6001, J604; default: on)");
 module_param(agx_vote_idle_ms, uint, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(agx_vote_idle_ms, "Keep the AGX request this many ms after the last GPU operation ends (default: 250)");
 
